-- Migration 4 -> 5: pin a friend's recovery public key (trust-on-first-use).
--
-- Until now `handleDeviceAnnounce` verified `DeviceAnnounce.signature` against
-- `DeviceAnnounce.recovery_public_key` — field 5 of the SAME peer-supplied message. That
-- authenticates nothing: anyone can generate a keypair, sign whatever they like with it, and ship
-- both halves. `client.proto` describes that field as the key "for friend to verify FUTURE
-- revocation signatures", i.e. a value the receiver LEARNS once and then holds the sender to. This
-- column is where it is held. ObscuraKit-swift's `friends` table already has it.
--
-- ALTER TABLE ADD COLUMN, deliberately, not a table rebuild: `SchemaMigrationTests.migrated schema
-- is identical to a freshly created one` compares the CREATE text SQLite stores in `sqlite_master`,
-- and a rebuild changes it (`ALTER TABLE ... RENAME TO` writes `CREATE TABLE "Friend"`, with
-- quotes). ADD COLUMN instead appends `, recovery_public_key BLOB` before the closing paren, which
-- is exactly what `Friend.sq` now declares — see the note there before reformatting either.
--
-- Nullable with no default on purpose: NULL means "nothing pinned yet", which is the state the
-- TOFU branch keys on. A default would make every existing friend look already-pinned.
ALTER TABLE Friend ADD COLUMN recovery_public_key BLOB;
